          "text": "## September 2025 Cost Activity Review\n\n- **Work order:** `WO-2025-09-004`\n- **Work order number:** `MO-25-09-1070`\n- **Cost event:** `CE-250904-0004`\n- **Event type:** `INPUT` — component issue\n- **Source transaction:** `TXN-ISSUE-250930-1070`\n- **Amount:** **28,476,342 cents** (**$284,763.42**)\n- **Exact event-created time:** `2025-09-30T19:15:00`\n- **Exact Pending Close time:** `2025-09-30T18:00:00`\n- **Late by:** **75 minutes**\n- **Recorded accounting status:** `POSTED`\n\n### Conclusion\n\nYes. The component-input event was created **75 minutes after** the September cost period entered Pending Close. Oracle’s documented treatment states that transactions created after Pending Close are not processed, except for revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments. Because this was an `INPUT`/component-issue transaction, its recorded `POSTED` status is **not consistent** with that policy.\n\nThe review was read-only; no database records were changed. The audit artifact was saved and the report submission was verified.",
